//! **The bridge**: a fully-applied recursor spine with a stuck major is
//! permanently ι-dead.
//!
//! The companion to `iota_immune_of_under_applied` (`stuck_recursor.rs`), which
//! closed the case where the major slot does not exist. This closes the case
//! where it exists and holds something that never becomes a constructor — the
//! half that module recorded as needing the confluence argument and left
//! unattempted.
//!
//! ## Why it is one entangled induction, not two composable halves
//!
//! The obvious plan is: prove the spine keeps its head and slot along a
//! reduction, then compose that with a refutation of the ι step. **That plan is
//! circular, and the preservation half is false on its own.** `par_reduces_cd`
//! carries `iota` as a **top-level** arm, so along `r =>* e2` some step may fire
//! ι at the top, after which `e2` is the rule body with an entirely different
//! head. Preservation holds only *given* that ι never fires — which is what the
//! bridge exists to prove.
//!
//! So the ι arm is refuted **in line**, using the invariant established so far.
//! Contrast `bvar_major_star_preserved`, which does separate cleanly: a `bvar`
//! major has no constant name, so its ι arm dies outright without consulting
//! the invariant. Here ι is ruled out only by `hno`, and `hno` needs
//! `maj =>* m2` — the invariant itself.
//!
//! ## The three layers
//!
//! ```text
//! stuck_major_step_inv  -- 11 arms of par_reduces_cd.rec; iota refuted in line
//! stuck_major_star_inv  -- 2 arms; chains the single step through the IH
//! iota_immune_of_stuck_major -- seeds the invariant at the spine, then refutes
//! ```
//!
//! `DerivedProved` throughout, empty axiom closures.

