impl Specification {
    /// The bridge, in three layers.
    pub(super) fn add_stuck_major_immune(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_STEP_INV, "stuck_major_step_inv: ONE parallel step out of a recursor spine with a stuck major preserves the head, the major slot, and the fact that the slot content is a REDUCT of the original major. Eleven arms of par_reduces_cd.rec. \
\
The iota arm is REFUTED rather than maintained, and that is what makes the whole thing work: this lemma cannot be split into preservation-then-composition, because par_reduces_cd carries iota as a TOP-LEVEL arm, so preservation holds only GIVEN that iota never fires. Refuting it in line, using the invariant established so far, is the resolution. \
\
Seven arms are literally option_none_ne_some_type: kapp_fn of a non-app returns the term and kexpr_const_name of it reduces to none, so the head hypothesis IS Eq none (some nm) definitionally, and no discrimination lemma is needed. refl hands the invariant back. app delegates to stuck_major_app_arm, delta to delta_dead_head_no_delta, iota to stuck_major_iota_arm_absurd. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_STAR_INV, "stuck_major_star_inv: the same invariant along ANY number of steps. Two arms over par_reduces_cd_star.rec -- refl hands it back, step chains the single-step lemma into the induction hypothesis. The CPS shape is what makes the chaining a one-liner: the single step is handed a continuation that feeds the IH. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IOTA_IMMUNE, "iota_immune_of_stuck_major: THE BRIDGE. A recursor spine whose major has no constructor-headed reduct with a matching rule is PERMANENTLY iota-dead. \
\
This is the fully-applied companion to iota_immune_of_under_applied, and the last thing on the def-eq completeness path that required proof discovery rather than assembly. Its hypothesis hno is exactly what the completed stuck-major classification supplies (stuck_major_confluence.rs for rigid/lam/dead-const, stuck_major_recmeta.rs for the recmeta-carrying case). \
\
The proof seeds the invariant at the spine itself -- the slot holds the major, which reduces to itself by refl -- runs it along the reduction with stuck_major_star_inv, and refutes the firing iota step with stuck_major_iota_arm_absurd at the reduct the invariant delivers. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_NEUTRAL_HEAD_DEAD, "iota_neutral_head_dead: an iota-neutral spine has a CONSTANT at its head, and that constant is delta-dead. CPS at C : Type because the consumers' goals are Type-valued. \
\
The extractor step 8 of the hnf3 chain needs, and it did not exist: iota_neutral_head_match is a HeadMatch lemma relating two spines, not a name extractor. Two arms. The const arm hands back its own name by Eq.refl -- kexpr_const_name (kapp_fn (const n us)) reduces to some n -- and converts its delta-deadness with defval_none_of_delta_reduct_none. The app arm just forwards to the induction hypothesis, because kapp_fn (app f a) unfolds to kapp_fn f, so the continuation at the sub-spine IS the continuation at the whole one. \
\
Note the UNITS: iota_neutral's const constructor carries delta-deadness as delta_reduct (const n us) = none, while the stuck-major classification lemmas want defval_for n = none. Those are equivalent but not identical, and the bridge in that direction already existed. Conflating them is the same class of near-miss that delta-dead-versus-head-none was on the delta arm. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_HNO_HEAD_NONE, "hno_of_head_none: THE k5 SUPPLIER. If the major's whnf has no constant at its head, the major has no constructor-headed reduct with a matching rule. Confluence yields a common reduct v headed by the constructor; nf_head_star_preserves_const_name carries the absent head name forward to v; contradiction. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_HNO_HEAD_NO_RULE, "hno_of_head_no_rule: THE k6 SUPPLIER. If the major's whnf is headed by cn2 and cn2 has NO rule under the recursor nm, the major has no constructor-headed reduct with a matching rule. Confluence yields v headed by cname, head preservation forces cn2 = cname, and the absent rule contradicts the present one. \
\
*** hnorule COMES FROM STUCKNESS, NOT FROM nf_head. *** A delta-dead RECMETA-FREE constant can perfectly well be a constructor carrying a rule under nm, in which case the whnf really IS constructor-headed and the conclusion is FALSE -- so no amount of nf_head information can supply hnorule. It is the iota chain's level-6 decline, handed over by iota_reduct_whc3_stuck_inv's k6 continuation. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        Ok(())
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    /// The iota arm must be refuted INSIDE the step lemma. If it were ever
    /// maintained instead, the lemma would be the non-entangled version, which
    /// is false: preservation holds only given that iota never fires.
    #[test]
    fn test_iota_is_refuted_inside_the_step_lemma() {
        assert!(
            SRC_STEP_INV.contains("stuck_major_iota_arm_absurd"),
            "the iota arm must be refuted in line, using the invariant so far"
        );
    }

    /// Every arm must be accounted for: 11 minor premises for par_reduces_cd.
    #[test]
    fn test_eleven_arms() {
        let arms = SRC_STEP_INV.matches("(k : forall (m2 : KExpr)").count();
        assert_eq!(
            arms, 11,
            "par_reduces_cd has 11 constructors; found {arms} arms"
        );
    }

    /// Seven arms discriminate, and must do so WITHOUT a discrimination lemma:
    /// `kexpr_const_name` of a non-app head reduces to `none`, so the head
    /// hypothesis already IS `Eq none (some nm)`. A `kexpr_discr_t` here would
    /// be seven avoidable transports.
    #[test]
    fn test_discriminating_arms_need_no_discrimination_lemma() {
        let kills = SRC_STEP_INV
            .matches("option_none_ne_some_type Name nm C hh")
            .count();
        assert_eq!(kills, 7, "beta, lam, pi, forall_, let_, let_cong, proj");
        assert!(
            !SRC_STEP_INV.contains("kexpr_discr_t"),
            "the head hypothesis is definitionally Eq none (some nm)"
        );
    }

    /// Each of the three delegating arms must reach its own lemma.
    #[test]
    fn test_delegating_arms_reach_their_lemmas() {
        for (arm, lemma) in [
            ("app", "stuck_major_app_arm"),
            ("delta", "delta_dead_head_no_delta"),
            ("iota", "stuck_major_iota_arm_absurd"),
        ] {
            assert!(
                SRC_STEP_INV.contains(lemma),
                "the {arm} arm must use {lemma}"
            );
        }
    }

    /// The capstone must seed the invariant with `refl` — the slot holds the
    /// major, which reduces to itself. Seeding it any other way would be
    /// assuming part of what is proved.
    #[test]
    fn test_capstone_seeds_the_invariant_by_refl() {
        assert!(
            SRC_IOTA_IMMUNE.contains("par_reduces_cd_star.refl the_red_env maj"),
            "the invariant starts with maj reducing to itself"
        );
        assert!(SRC_IOTA_IMMUNE.contains("stuck_major_star_inv"));
    }

    /// The extractor must convert units, not assume them: `iota_neutral` gives
    /// `delta_reduct = none` and the consumers want `defval_for = none`.
    #[test]
    fn test_head_extractor_converts_the_deadness_units() {
        assert!(
            SRC_NEUTRAL_HEAD_DEAD.contains("defval_none_of_delta_reduct_none"),
            "delta_reduct = none and defval_for = none are equivalent, not identical"
        );
    }

    /// The app arm forwards to the IH with no transport, because
    /// `kapp_fn (app f a)` unfolds to `kapp_fn f`. If a transport ever appears
    /// there, the definitional unfolding was missed.
    #[test]
    fn test_extractor_app_arm_forwards_directly() {
        assert!(
            SRC_NEUTRAL_HEAD_DEAD.contains("=> ih C2 kont2)"),
            "kapp_fn (app f a) unfolds to kapp_fn f, so the continuation carries over as-is"
        );
    }

    /// Both hno suppliers correspond to the inverter's two live continuations,
    /// and both must go through head preservation — that is what carries the
    /// whnf's head fact forward to the common reduct.
    #[test]
    fn test_hno_suppliers_use_head_preservation() {
        for src in [SRC_HNO_HEAD_NONE, SRC_HNO_HEAD_NO_RULE] {
            assert!(src.contains("nf_head_star_preserves_const_name"));
            assert!(src.contains("stuck_major_join_ctor_head_at_the_red_env"));
        }
    }

    /// `hnorule` must be a PREMISE of the k6 supplier. It cannot come from
    /// `nf_head`: a δ-dead, recmeta-free constant can be a constructor carrying
    /// a rule, and then the conclusion is false. It is level-6 stuckness data.
    #[test]
    fn test_k6_takes_the_absent_rule_as_a_premise() {
        assert!(SRC_HNO_HEAD_NO_RULE.contains("(hnorule : Eq (OptionType RecRule)"));
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_sources_balanced_ascii_prime_free() {
        for src in [
            SRC_STEP_INV,
            SRC_STAR_INV,
            SRC_IOTA_IMMUNE,
            SRC_NEUTRAL_HEAD_DEAD,
            SRC_HNO_HEAD_NONE,
            SRC_HNO_HEAD_NO_RULE,
        ] {
            let mut depth: i64 = 0;
            for ch in src.chars() {
                match ch {
                    '(' => depth += 1,
                    ')' => depth -= 1,
                    _ => {}
                }
                assert!(depth >= 0, "close paren before its open");
            }
            assert_eq!(depth, 0, "unbalanced parens");
            assert!(src.is_ascii());
            assert!(!src.contains('\''));
        }
    }
}
